{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "10", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "10", "M": "55", "S": "18"}}, "news": [{"title": "About 66% mutation cases disposed of online: Bihar revenue minister", "para": "The integration of online revenue services and departmental oversight has significantly expedited the resolution of land cases. In the period of 2026-27, 66% of mutation cases and 31% of Maha-Abhiyan applications were effectively resolved. A surge of over five lakh online mutation applications was processed, and digitized Jamabandi records facilitated the disposal of more than six lakh cases through Parimarjan Plus.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/technology/about-66-mutation-cases-disposed-of-online-bihar-revenue-minister/133089227?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-111836/133089227.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "technology"}, {"title": "Indore: 8.5% rise in property registrations in last four months", "para": "Indore's real estate market has witnessed a thriving boost, with property transactions rising by 8.5 percent, generating significant revenue for the state. The expansion of outer corridors and emerging zones is driving this surge. Interestingly, property sales in older, central regions are experiencing a slight downturn. Overall, this trend highlights a strong rebound in the local property sector.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/indore-8-5-rise-in-property-registrations-in-last-four-months/133088554?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-104236/133088554.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Nagpur: 88% of buildings lack OCs, union minister sets four-month deadline to resolve issue", "para": "Nearly eighty-eight percent of Nagpur's buildings lack mandatory Occupancy Certificates. Union minister Nitin Gadkari directed notices for pending issues within four months. Registrations of independent houses will continue under existing legal rules. Confusion arose over building permission certificates and Occupancy Certificates for large buildings. Developers failing to obtain Occupancy Certificates will not be allowed property registration.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/nagpur-88-of-buildings-lack-ocs-union-minister-sets-four-month-deadline-to-resolve-issue/133088420?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-136712/133088420.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}]}